  "title": "New Testament core: verbs",
  "note": "Each of these verbs occurs 50 times or more in the New Testament. Many are compounds: a preposition joined to a simple verb, as ἔρχομαι 'I go' gives εἰσ-έρχομαι 'I go in', ἐξ-έρχομαι 'I go out', ἀπ-έρχομαι 'I go away' and προσ-έρχομαι 'I come to'. Learn the simple verb and the prepositions, and the compounds become easy to read.",
